@startuml
title JCB Render Command Flow (jcb render temp.yaml dest.yaml)


participant "jcb (CLI)" as CLI
participant "driver.py" as Driver
participant "renderer.py" as Renderer
participant "Jinja2 Engine" as Jinja2
database "temp.yaml" as InputYAML
database "dest.yaml" as OutputYAML
collections "Templates (.j2)" as Templates

skinparam handwritten true
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 20
skinparam maxmessagesize 120
skinparam sequenceParticipant bordercolor DarkSlateGray
skinparam sequenceActor bordercolor DarkSlateGray



CLI -> Driver: main()
activate Driver

Driver -> InputYAML: Reads `temp.yaml`
activate InputYAML
InputYAML --> Driver: Returns template dictionary
deactivate InputYAML

Driver -> Renderer: Calls [render(template_dict)]\n (src/jcb/renderer.py\n:174:4-240:24)
activate Renderer

Renderer -> Renderer: new Renderer(template_dict)
note right: Initializes Jinja2 search paths\nbased on the input dictionary.

Renderer -> Renderer: Calls internal [render(algorithm)]\n(src/jcb/renderer.py\n:174:4-240:24)
Renderer -> Jinja2: env.get_template\n(algorithm + '.yaml.j2')
activate Jinja2

Jinja2 -> Templates: Loads main template and any includes
activate Templates
Templates --> Jinja2: Returns template contents
deactivate Templates

Jinja2 -> Jinja2: Renders templates using variables\nfrom `template_dict`
Jinja2 --> Renderer: Returns final YAML as a string
deactivate Jinja2

Renderer -> Renderer: Loads YAML string into a dictionary
Renderer --> Driver: Returns final dictionary
deactivate Renderer

Driver -> OutputYAML: Writes dictionary to `dest.yaml`
activate OutputYAML
OutputYAML --> Driver: Success
deactivate OutputYAML

Driver --> CLI: Returns
deactivate Driver



@enduml

